   The total volume of the final solution is 20.0 L, and the molarity is 3.00 M.
   \[
   \text{Moles in 20.0 L of 3.00 M solution} = 3.00 \text{ M} \times 20.0 \text{ L} = 60.0 \text{ moles}
   \]
   The sum of the moles from the two solutions should equal the total moles:
   \[
   10.0 + 6.00V = 60.0
   \]

