The pH of a solution is calculated using the formula:  
\[
\text{pH} = -\log[H_3O^+]
\]  
Given \([H_3O^+] = 10^{-4}\) M, the pH is:  
\[
\text{pH} = -\log(10^{-4}) = -(-4) = 4
\]  
A solution is:  
- Aconic if \(\text{pH} < 7\)  
- Neutral if \(\text{pH} = 7\)  
- Basic if \(\text{pH} > 7\)  
Since the pH is \(\boxed{4}\), the solution is \(\boxed{\text{acetic}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

