     \[
     \nabla \times \mathbf{H} = \mathbf{J} = 0, \quad \text{since there is no current density in the medium.}
     \]
     By symmetry, \( \mathbf{H} \) must be of the form \( \mathbf{H} = H_0(r) \hat{\varphi} \), where \( \hat{\varphi} \) is the azimuthal unit vector.
