The reaction in case is the oxidation of the amine group (-NH2) to a nitrogen molecule (N2), with the presence of the pentantrioaneline bonding to the bond between the two carbon atoms, forming the benzene molecule. This reaction is essential for converting the amphic acid molecule into the benzene molecule. The reaction is typically performed in a strong acid medium, such as sulfide acid or perfirfric acid.

