$$ a_6 = a_1 + (6 - 1)d = 19 + 5d. $$
The term $a_6$ is the first term that becomes negative, so $a_6 < 0$.
$$ 19 + 5d < 0 \implies 5d < -19 \implies d < -\frac{19}{5} \implies d < -3.8. $$
Since the common difference is an integer, $d \leq -4$.

The term $a_5$ is positive, so $a_5 > 0$:
$$ a_5 = a_1 + (5 - 1)d = 19 + 4d > 0 \implies 4d > -19 \implies d > -\frac{19}{4} \implies d > -4.75. $$
Since the common difference is an integer, $d \geq -4$.

Combining the two conditions, we have $-4.75 < d < -3.8$. Since $d$ is an integer, the only possible value for $d$ is $-4$.

Thus, the common difference is $-4$.

