   \[
   \cos (180^\circ + \alpha) = -\cos \alpha, \quad \sin (\alpha + 360^\circ) = \sin \alpha,
   \]
   \[
   \sin (-\alpha - 180^\circ) = \sin (-180^\circ - \alpha) = -\sin (\alpha + 180^\circ) = -\cos \alpha,
   \]
   \[
   \cos (-180^\circ - \alpha) = -\cos (\alpha + 180^\circ) = \cos \alpha.
   \]
   Substituting these into the expression:
   \[
   \boxed{\frac{(-\cos \alpha) \cdot \sin \alpha}{(-\cos \alpha) \cdot \cos \alpha}} = \frac{-\cos \alpha \sin \alpha}{-\cos^2 \alpha} = \frac{\sin \alpha}{\cos \alpha} = \tan \alpha.
