   \mathcal{F} \left[ \sin(\omega_0 t) \right] = \frac{\omega_0}{\pi} \left[ \delta(f - \omega_0) - \delta(f + \omega_0) \right].
   \]
   For \( \omega_0 = 2\pi \), we have:
   \[
   \mathcal{F} \left[ \sin(2\pi t) \right] = \frac{2\pi}{\pi} \left[ \delta(f - 2\pi) - \delta(f + 2\pi) \right] = 2 \left[ \delta(f - 2\pi) - \delta(f + 2\pi) \right].
   \]

