\]
Now, compute the first derivative:
\[
\frac{d}{dx} \left( x^6 - 3x^4 + 3x^2 - 1 \right) = 6x^5 - 12x^3 + 6x
\]
Compute the second derivative:
\[
\frac{d^2}{dx^2} \left( 6x^5 - 12x^3 + 6x \right) = 30x^4 - 36x^2 + 6
\]
Compute the third derivative:
\[
\frac{d^3}{dx^3} \left( 30x^4 - 36x^2 + 6 \right) = 120x^3 - 72x
