\[
V_T = \sqrt{\frac{2E_g}{3}} \left( \frac{k_T}{q} \right) + \frac{q N_A \phi_f}{k_T} - \frac{q^2}{2 \epsilon_{ox} t_{ox}} \left( \frac{N_D + N_A}{2} \right)
\]

where:
- \(E_g\) is the bandgap energy of silicon (\(1.12 \text{ eV}\))
- \(k_T = \frac{q}{2\pi m_e} \approx 0.0257 \text{ eV/K}\) (at 300 K)
- \(q\) is the elementary charge (\(1.6 \times 10^{-19} \text{ C}\))
- \(N_A\) is the acceptor doping concentration in the p-type region
- \(\phi_f\) is the Fermi potential
- \(\epsilon_{ox}\) is the permittivity of silicon dioxide (\(3.4 \times 10^{-11} \text{ F/m}\))
- \(t_{ox}\) is the oxide thickness
- \(N_D\) is the donor doping concentration in the n-type gate region

