\]
This is derived from the equation for the imaginary part of the coupling constant \(k_f\) for total internal reflection:
\[
\frac{1}{l} = \frac{1}{2\pi} \sqrt{n_{\text{core}}^2 - n_{\text{clad}}^2} \frac{2\pi}{\lambda}.
\]
The refractive indices of GaAs and Ga\(_{0.2}\)Al\(_{0.8}\)As at 1 μm are approximately:
- \(n_{\text{GaAs}} \approx 3.36\)
- \(n_{\text{GaAsAl}} \approx 3.1\)

The refractive index difference is \(n_{\text{core}} - n_{\text{clad}} \approx 0.3\). 

Thus, the decay length \(l\) is:
\[
\frac{1}{l} = \frac{2\pi}{\lambda} \sqrt{n_{\text{core}}^2 - n_{\text{clad}}^2}.
\]
Substituting \(n_{\text{core}} - n_{\text{clad}} = 0.3\) and \(\lambda = 1 \, \mu\text{m} = 10^{-6} \, \text{m}\):
\[
\frac{1}{l} = \frac{2\pi}{10^{-6}} \sqrt{n_{\text{core}}^2 - (n_{\text{core}} - 0.3)^2}.
\]
\[
\frac{1}{l} = \frac{2\pi}{10^{-6}} \sqrt{n_{\text{core}^2} - (n_{\text{core}}^2 - 0.6n_{\text{core}} + 0.09)}.
