","The study of non-perturbative effects in quantum field theory can be achieved through several techniques, such as the instanton and soliton approaches. These effects are essential for a complete description of physical phenomena, as they account for phenomena that perturbative methods, which extend the theory as a power series in the coupling constant, typically treat as irrelevant.

